name duel-headon-1
timeout 600

# THE ASYMMETRIC DUEL, GEOMETRY 1 OF 8: HEAD-ON. The reference case of the campaign
# (doc/duels.md) and the one in which the two weapon systems differ most sharply.
#
# WHAT IS ASYMMETRIC, and none of it is mission data — it is what the two modules ARE:
#   detection   APG-68 40 nm gate against a 4.0 m^2 MiG = 100 km; N019 RAD 27 nm against a 1.2 m^2
#               F-16 = 50 km. The fourth-root RCS law (sensors/FBRadarSystem::GateRangeM) hands the
#               F-16 the first look by a factor of two, before either pilot decides anything.
#   weapon      AIM-120 active: the shooter's obligation ends at the activation ring. R-27R
#               semi-active: the obligation runs to IMPACT (weapons.md, FBSeekerHandoverS = -1),
#               and pilot/FBPilot's SupportInhibitsDefend hook makes the MiG's phase machine obey it.
#   defence     ALE-47 against nothing. The MiG-29 has no dispenser in FlightBox
#               (modules/mig29/module.md gap 4g), so its only answer to a radar shot is the beam.
#
# BOTH SIDES FLY THE SAME PHASE MACHINE with their own numbers, and nothing is scripted: no briefed
# release, no briefed chaff, no briefed manoeuvre. Each jet gets a vector and a master-arm call.
#
# GEOMETRY: 111 km apart at 46.90 N, co-altitude 8,000 m, head-on, both outside BOTH radar gates at
# t=0 so both runs begin with a real search phase.
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 (TIMEOUT), both alive — and that IS the measured answer rather than a missing
# one. Both pilots ship with the SAME doctrine (designate at the airframe's lock range, shoot at Rtr),
# both reach it within 1.4 s of each other, both shoot, and every round arrives outside its warhead's
# lethal radius. MEASURED: viper detects at t=24.0 (52.1 nm) against fulcrum's t=105.2 (26.0 nm) — an
# 81 s lead that is pure sensor physics (40 nm gate x 1.351 for a 4.0 m^2 target = 100 km, against
# 27 nm x 1.0 for a 1.2 m^2 one = 50 km) — and then the lead evaporates, because both trigger gates sit
# at Rtr and Rtr is a function of the GEOMETRY both share: 9.78 nm for the AIM-120, 10.25 for the
# R-27R, reached at t=156.6 and t=155.2. Two AIM-120s arrive 7.52 m and 8.83 m out, the R-27R runs out
# of flight time 14.96 m out, and a 20.5 kg warhead at 7.5 m wrecks avionics without taking the engine,
# the flight controls or the structure (core/FBDamageModel's 1/r^2).
#
# WHAT THE DRAW SAYS, and it is the campaign's central result: the F-16's radar advantage is real and
# it buys a detection, not a kill. What decides is the SHOT, and to make the shot decide, one side has
# to stop flying the other's doctrine (duel-doctrine-mig.fbm) or bring energy to it
# (duel-doctrine-f16.fbm). exit 2 (CRASH) would be a defect.
#
# MEASURE, side by side in telemetry.csv (viper) and telemetry_fulcrum.csv:
#   eng_detect_s / eng_lock_s     who saw whom first, and at what range
#   eng_shot_s / eng_shot_nm      who shot first, and out of what launch envelope (eng_shot_rtr_nm)
#   eng_support_s / eng_support_f the SARH penalty as a number: the MiG's window is the whole time of
#                                 flight, the F-16's ends at the seeker
#   eng_state                     the two machines interleaved; the MiG's SUPPORT_BINDING lines are
#                                 the ticks in which it was NOT allowed to defend
#   dmg_failed / dmg_effective    what arrived

unit viper
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 6.40000 8000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink off                         # a fight is fought on own sensors
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set store 8 aim9                         # selected only after both AMRAAMs are gone (station step)
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 46.90000 8.40000 8000 450
  objective kill unit fulcrum
  objective survive

unit fulcrum
  team hostile
  module mig29
  spawn 46.90000 7.85000 8000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad                        # the wide non-locking search pattern
  set n019_range_nm 27                     # the set's own documented search reach
  set n019_emission illum                  # LOUD from t=0: the baseline against which duel-emcon reads
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set store 5 r73                          # station step reaches it after both R-27Rs
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 46.90000 5.85000 8000 450
  objective kill unit viper
  objective survive
